# https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp#Product> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Any raw, semi-worked, worked, semi-manufactured, manufactured, semi-made-up or made-up product which is exclusively composed of textile fibres, as well as a product containing at least 80% textile fibres by weight."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Textile product"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "TextileProduct is the broad textile product class. It includes final products and products serving an intermediate or component role when they are represented as product-like traceability resources. Identification constraints should be specified by SHACL according to product granularity rather than imposed uniformly on every TextileProduct."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-core#TextileProduct> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Preparatory Study, relevant section, printed page 14, lines 161-166."@en .
