<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#WeavePatternSpecification> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "The JRC identifies weave pattern as one of the weaving parameters affecting fabric characteristics. The relation is represented as weak influence annotations rather than as deterministic OWL axioms."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#WeavePatternSpecification> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "The process-side target remains distinct from the resulting characteristic represented in Textile Structure."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-process#WeavePatternSpecification> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "Weave pattern is a fabric construction parameter that may affect visual appearance, permeability, drape and handle. The relation is represented as weak influence because the direction depends on the specific weave and yarns."@en .
