# https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreQualityCharacteristic> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> <https://susproc.jrc.ec.europa.eu/product-bureau/sites/default/files/2025-12/Textile-Prep-Study_3rd-Milestone_20251212.pdf> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Fibre quality characteristic concerning impurities or foreign matter remaining in the fibre."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Fibre cleanliness"@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "The term is named FibreCleanliness rather than FibreCleanness, following standard textile and English usage."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#evidenceStatus> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#explicitEvidence> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "A weak influence link from fibre cleanliness to yarn appearance is represented in this module. The corresponding link to fabric appearance remains pending until a fabric appearance target concept is introduced."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#modellingNote> "Fibre cleanliness is modelled as a fibre quality characteristic, not as a structural dimension such as length, fineness or section shape. Quantitative or qualitative measurements of contamination, trash content or impurity levels should be represented through assessment results."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceLocator> "JRC Section 9.2.1, printed page 110, lines 2895-2900; Annex 13.10.2, Tables 177 and 180, printed pages 486-491; captions at lines 11873 and 11879; supporting text on printed page 484, lines 11853-11859."@en .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#sourceType> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#adaptedDefinition> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#typicalInfluenceOn> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FabricAppearance> .
<https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#FibreCleanliness> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-connector#typicalInfluenceOn> <https://w3id.org/eudpp/textile-structure#YarnAppearance> .
